WHATNOW

What tam-clam is doing now and what comes next. Read this first; revise
it at the end of every session (work/README-work).

Updated: 2026-11-23, with W13 (0.1.5)


STATE

  Version 0.1.5, Phase P2 COMPLETE (full POSIX.1-2024 shell language,
  builtins, options, spec suite, fuzzing, and lint mode), on branch dev.
  0.1.5 adds:
  - 1-based column tracking across input.c, lex.c, ast.h, and parse.c;
  - static lint mode (`tam-clam --lint FILE...`) in
    include/tam-clam/lint.h and src/lint.c: parses with the real parser,
    runs nothing, emits `file:line:col: warning [check-name]: message`
    (exit 0 clean, 1 warnings, 2 syntax/I/O error);
  - checks: unquoted-test, unquoted-case, unchecked-cd, unquoted-star,
    split-cmdsub, and unset-var, with inline and preceding-line
    `# lint: allow <name>` suppression comments;
  - tests/test_lint.c, --lint CLI checks in tests/run-scripts.sh, and
    sandbox/demo-0.1.5-lint added to sandbox/play.
  readelf -d lists only libc.so.6. make test and make sanitize pass.

  Fred's decisions so far are in ROADMAP.md and the plans: POSIX.1-2024
  is the target; lint mode is P2 0.1.5 (done); the Tamlinux-wide
  keybinding standard lives in tamlinux/arch/keybindings.md (settled
  2026-11-23) and tam-clam's arch/keys.md is drafted against it (W13,
  no vi mode, no built-in readline map, VINTR=Ctrl+\, VSUSP=Ctrl+P,
  Ctrl+F history search, Ctrl+Q quit); FUNCNEST sets the function
  recursion limit; signed 64-bit arithmetic overflow is a reported
  error; echo recognizes -n only and does not interpret backslash
  escapes by default.


